+// flow_try_spawn — the 3.3 spawn entry: flow_spawn with the E22
+// pool-exhaustion guard. When the global in-flight pool is at its cap
+// (pool_max_packets), the drop ladder engages over the pool — the shed
+// target is the NEWEST packet of the LOWEST-priority non-empty lane (BE →
+// Standard → Express). The arrival is admitted ONLY when the target is
+// STRICTLY lower priority than its own lane (a lower-priority resident
+// pays); otherwise the arriving packet drops — it is the lowest-priority
+// candidate present (the inversion guard: an Express resident NEVER pays
+// for a Standard arrival). Drops emit Packet_Dropped{class,
+// Pool_Exhaustion}. Returns true when the packet spawned.
+flow_try_spawn :: proc(state: ^Run_State, cat: ^Catalogs, class: u16, src, dst: u32, tick: u64) -> bool {
+	f := &state.flow
